--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,6 +9,26 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Local connections
+
+Open **Local connections** in the footer (`/devtools-times/local-connections`).
+The page reads JSON status from a LAN device or a loopback companion app using
+separate permissions. Replace the example URLs with your service's status URL.
+No companion service is bundled with this application.
+
+Serve the application over HTTPS (for example, behind a TLS reverse proxy).
+The controls intentionally refuse to connect from HTTP, including HTTP localhost.
+The device or companion service must allow the application's origin through
+standard CORS response headers. No deprecated private-network preflight headers
+are needed. A browser without permission-query support still requires a click.
+
+Run the browser regression tests with `npx playwright install chromium` followed
+by `npm run test:lna`. To use an existing Chrome installation, set
+`PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH` to its executable path instead.
+The tests build and serve the app, then exercise it under an HTTPS test origin
+with mocked device responses and permission states. Testing actual browser
+permission prompts requires an HTTPS public origin and a running local service.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
